WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.260
We're almost finished
with our game's production.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.980
It's going to only get more
intense toward the end.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.590
But I hope you can all stick
with it to the end.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.190
Once we get through this, it'll be finished.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.990
Okay, let's do this! Yeah!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.450
Yeah!

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.790
We need three more BGM tracks...

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.540
The final third of the script...

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.580
But a whole fourth of the illustrations...

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.750
We're going to have to make
some big cuts to finish in time.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.330
But I've already had them
put up with so much.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.300
I keep remembering what happened before.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.390
If the alternative
is going through that again...

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.780
No! Things are different now!

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.350
We have to finish this game!
For Tsurayuki's sake!

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.000
You want me to make it just
like this? What do you mean?

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.830
I realize we can't just rip off the melody,

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.730
but I'd like you to try something
with a similar feel.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.030
I get it...

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:38.220
Well, considering I'm behind already,
I guess we don't have a choice.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.390
We won't be able to call this
a 100% Nanako original.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.070
But I'd like you to do it
this way. Is that all right?

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:46.980
That works!

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.100
This might be a fun method to try, anyway.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.480
Thank you.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.940
You wanna change the layouts?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.750
Yeah.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:58.110
Since this material is for the climax,
I'd like you to make it a priority.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.560
A lot of these look the same.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.160
Is that gonna be okay?

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:07.370
Yeah. I want there to be a lot of emphasis
on the character faces in the finale,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.750
and this works better for that.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.840
Is that how it is?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:14.130
It'll be okay! So I'd like you to draw
to match these directions.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.500
Can you do that for me?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.380
Yeah! Sure thing.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.760
I'll do it your way, Kyoya-kun.
Let's see how it turns out.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.540
That's two people convinced.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.170
One more to go...

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.720
Kyoya, you expect me
to just write it like it says here?

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.080
I know that I'm behind.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:35.340
But, man... this is nothing
like the plot I wrote!

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.940
It's a whole different thing!

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:40.680
I know this won't take as long to write.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.730
And that's why I want to do it
this way, so we can make sure—

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.160
But if we do it that way...

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.910
Is there any point in me
being the one who writes it?

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.790
Tsurayuki...

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.080
You come up with the plot.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.950
You come up with
the setup for the finale.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.760
Where do I even factor into the equation?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.330
Don't be ridiculous.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:05.050
The entire feel of the game is
because of you writing it, Tsurayuki!

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.460
Even though I'm just doing
what you tell me to?

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.820
Of course.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:14.720
In commercial games, the director
handles the plot a lot of the time.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.110
Only a handful of writers are free to do
everything by themselves from the start.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.820
R-Really?

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.790
That's right.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.130
Besides, right now, we need to finish
in order to sell the game at the event!

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.120
That has to be our number one priority!

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:32.290
I realize I'm asking you to do
something unpleasant.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.490
But this was the best plan
I could come up with

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.880
to make sure we finish on time.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.580
Kyoya...

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:45.380
That's why I'm asking you to trust me,
and follow the directions.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.260
Okay. You've got it.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.150
You've always been right.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.420
And you're doing this
for my sake, after all.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.580
I appreciate it, Tsurayuki.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:05.900
For a brighter future...
we'll need to compromise, for now.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.880
You're right about that.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.240
The issues with the script
have been settled.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.000
We should be able to move
on to voice recording this week.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.980
Sounds good! Hard to believe
you guys were so far behind.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.210
The illustrations are coming in
at a better clip now, too.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.960
You use some kinda magic or something?

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.200
I just asked everyone
to prioritize progress.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.970
They all understood.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.340
Yeah? Well, whatever works.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:33.810
Now we just gotta get scaredy-cat
over there to chill out some.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:37.910
Oh, no, no, I am so nervous, oh man...

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:41.560
I thought the school festival's concert
would've been way more nerve-wracking.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:46.200
Eh, girls like her tend to be pretty tough
once they're actually in the fire.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.400
Huh...

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.320
Okay, that's good!

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.700
Very nice, Nanako-chan!

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.080
That felt fantastic!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.030
Can we do another take?

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:56.340
That works for me!

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.330
For this one, let's go with
a more energetic take.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.570
Okay!

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.650
What'd I tell you?

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.840
Fair enough.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.820
You did fantastic, Nanako!

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:10.930
The audio director was freaking out,
asking me where I found you!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.110
Come on, you have to be exaggerating.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.460
I'm looking forward to seeing
how things wrap up, now!

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.320
I'm glad we decided to do things my way.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.270
It was the right decision.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:21.810
I'm Kawasegawa. It's nice to meet you.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:22.850
I'm Kiryu.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.150
I'm the president of the
Fine Arts Study Group.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.860
Thank for letting us use
your computer again.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.870
Do you have a good idea of how
to use the editing software?

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.540
I've used Primia before,

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.770
but I'm not too familiar with After Affex...

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:40.330
I'll explain the differences
that matter, then.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:50.530
Uh, Hashy, is this girl some kinda
super honor student?

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:52.050
Yes, I'd say so.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.450
I figured!

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.570
She picked up what
I was putting down really quick.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:57.250
Was it really that impressive?

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:02.060
If she sticks to doing this, she'll be
one hell of a video editor someday.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:07.300
I guess her involvement in the game
industry happened pretty naturally.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.620
Hate to bug you
when you're working and all...

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.550
It's okay. What'd you want to talk about?

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.800
I came up with something great!

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.710
I wanted to get your take
as soon as possible!

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.880
These are the layouts
for the last cut, right?

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.680
You got it! I was thinking we
could make a little addition.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:27.460
An addition?

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:32.040
The script Tsurayuki-kun came up
with for this part was real good!

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:35.100
So I wanted to add another cut.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.850
The boy's line here is just great!

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:41.850
So I thought it'd be a good idea to put
his hand into the frame for that part.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.850
Because of his habit, right?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.060
Whenever he's being really
serious about something,

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:48.190
he always clenches his fist.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.230
Yeah! I thought we could emphasize it!

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.780
Additional art, huh?

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.210
It's a good idea.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.950
But the schedule for illustrations
is already falling apart.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:03.600
Additional art just isn't realistic.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.670
As a creator, I'd love
to sign off on this.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.030
But right now, considering our situation...

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:13.070
I think we're better off not changing it.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.160
How come?

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.280
I think it'd be way better,
with how the scene goes.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.520
You don't think it'd be ready in time?

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.940
It's not that.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:27.370
I want to put an emphasis on the expressions
you draw for this scene, Shinoaki.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:28.710
Expressions?

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:31.780
The other CG are only used
for two lines apiece.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.760
But this one has four.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.490
It's set up that way to put an emphasis
on how expressive she's being.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.250
I guess... that's right.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.980
Which is why, although I think
your change is an interesting one,

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.670
it'd still be better to go
with what we already have.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:48.920
What do you say?

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.970
Okay. I'll draw it the way
it was already set up.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:58.680
I'm sorry. You came up with a good idea.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.260
Nah. Sorry to bug you
when you're already real busy.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.710
This is for the best.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:08.100
This is the best choice,
for Tsurayuki's sake.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.640
Guys, this is the actual final stretch!

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.530
Once we're done we can
all sleep, so hang in there!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.720
Damn it! Another typo!

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.540
What the hell is wrong with my writing?!

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.320
Tsurayuki, I know you want to fix it,

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.370
but focus on debugging the game first!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.300
Y-Yeah, sorry.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:35.170
It's 2:00 AM... we have to take the master
to the printers at 10:00 AM.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.630
That gives us eight hours.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.180
Hey, everybody.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.610
Perfect timing!

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.930
Could you test the game out
on my PC on the second floor?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:46.560
You'll want to make the decisions
that will put you on her route!

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.380
O-Okay, then!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.270
Wh-What is it, Nanako?!

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:55.320
Th-The space where the expression was
supposed to be went all blank and smooth!

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.760
That's a bug!

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.080
Make a save there. I'll tell
Keiko-san about it later.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.540
G-Got it!

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.410
How are things on your end, Shinoaki?!

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:07.210
I was playing, but then
the screen went all black!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.870
That means the game crashed!

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.210
I'll tell Keiko-san about
that too, so leave it!

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.460
Hey, look at the busy bees.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:17.000
Oh, hell, we've got some
trouble in paradise, huh?

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.430
Yes! Can you help us with it?

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.510
Oh, yeah! Leave it to me.

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:26.300
I think there was a display problem
with the expression for that scene.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.210
That's gonna be rough.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.580
It might be good to review all of the routes.

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:32.170
Wait, really?!

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:35.480
Have everybody quit doing what
they're doing and focus on that for now.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.090
Shinoaki, restart the computer

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.080
and run through that route again,
while checking the art!

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.410
Okay, sure thing!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.750
You too, Kawasegawa,
you can skip through the dialog

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.070
but make sure to check
the art's displaying!

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:51.970
The game already crashed
when I got to a branching decision.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.960
That ain't good.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.730
Might need to review
a little further back, then.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:57.760
Oh, no...

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.050
How did I make a typo here, too?!

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.600
Now half the background's missing!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.640
Kyoya-kun, the whole dang
computer's crashed this time!

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.680
Hashiba, what do you
want me to do about this?

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.790
Everyone, stay calm!

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.950
I'm begging you!

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.190
Okay, that should do it...

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.740
Thank you so much. Here it is.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:24.120
Got it. I'm outta here, then.

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:28.330
Good work... team?

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:39.740
And so, our game was complete.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:44.440
But... I still had an important job left.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.850
To actually sell the game.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.350
Naw, I think it'll sell just fine.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:53.350
But we haven't really done any PR
since the initial announcement.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:56.910
For this game, as long as the
outside looks appealing enough,

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.900
the inside could be crap
and it'd still sell.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.320
That's the kinda position you're in.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.820
You think so?

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.730
You'll see.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.160
Another five minutes
until the shutters go up...

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.730
What, you still worried?

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:14.800
Yeah...

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:19.070
Look, however it happened,
you kids made something.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:22.380
And you're gonna see the response it gets.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.550
Okay.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.390
All right, here it comes.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:28.310
Okay, the event is now opening!

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:43.900
See? What'd I tell you?

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:50.620
All right, to the completion
and successful distribution of HaruSora.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.120
Cheers!

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:55.090
It's over... It's finally done.

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.240
I don't ever wanna ever
look for typos again.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:59.330
I was drawing and drawing,
and it never ended.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.380
I kinda thought it never would.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.680
All of you did an absolutely
amazing job! Thank you!

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:08.680
This entire project only came
together because of all of you!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:12.430
We couldn't have finished
if it wasn't for you, Kyoya.

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:13.690
That's right.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:17.450
We couldn't have managed
a dang thing without Kyoya-kun.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:20.870
We were practically leaving
all the decisions to him.

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:22.110
And it worked out, thanks to Kyoya!

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:26.010
Aw, c-come on... Cut it out. It's not true.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.610
Oh, Kyoya? Are those tears I see?

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:30.590
N-No, of course not!

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.360
You worked a bunch,
so you're bound to be tired.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:36.620
You can get some rest now.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.470
Yeah. She's right.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:43.000
I was filled with an irrepressible joy.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:47.130
I wanted to keep making
things with this team.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:50.880
I went ten years into the past,
and chose to become a creator...

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.470
And I'm so glad.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.640
This should be enough, right?

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:58.270
Everyone was having a lot of fun, huh?

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.430
They probably feel relieved.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:03.900
Tsurayuki and Nanako both looked like a
weight had been lifted off their shoulders.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:07.150
Yeah. There's no need to hang tough anymore.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:10.910
We chose our battles, finished our work,
and achieved our goal with it.

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:14.520
We'll be able to do even
more things, from here on.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.160
Both in class, and in creating... and then...

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:21.010
Say, Shinoaki, what do you—

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:22.540
Y'know, Kyoya-kun...

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.050
Is this really how it oughta be?

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:32.750
How it ought to be? What do you mean?

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:37.420
It just... feels like I should ask.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:39.800
It... was a success.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:44.150
I mean, we all worked hard
to help Tsurayuki, right?

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:48.070
Yeah. In that case, it's fine.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:50.700
Sorry for asking such a weird thing.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.950
No, you don't have to worry about it.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.950
Let me know if you're
feeling tired, you hear?

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.490
I...

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:04.340
will always believe in you, Kyoya-kun.

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:06.130
Right.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:09.420
I'm okay. Thank you.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.430
Okay, it's time to pass out
our share of the profits.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.430
Are we... really allowed
to have all this money?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.430
Kogure Nanako

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.850
This is great!

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:21.650
Shino Aki

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:21.650
It's gonna help a lot around the house.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.560
Rokuonji Tsurayuki

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:27.400
This takes care of your problem, Tsurayuki.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:31.820
Yeah. It's finally over now...

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.270
What're you saying? It's only beginning.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:36.600
Listen, Kyoya...

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:40.340
You wanna take a walk?

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:46.080
Whenever I had writer's block,
I'd walk around here.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.210
There's this little park.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:52.620
I'd sit there and brainstorm.

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.820
Are we gonna go there now?

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.970
Nah, this should do.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:00.000
If I went somewhere
with a lot of memories...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.920
I don't know if I'd be able to say it.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:10.150
I'm dropping out of school.

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:17.610
I'm really sorry, considering how
you busted your ass for me.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:21.240
The three of you can split
my share. I don't need it.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:23.810
What are you saying?

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.170
What the hell are you
talking about, Tsurayuki?!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.470
I thought you wanted to study!

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:31.210
This money was supposed to make that happen!

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:35.230
And because... because it was
too much to take care of on your own...

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:37.050
That's why... why I...

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:42.160
You can hit me, Kyoya. You've earned it.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:46.720
I just... can't do this anymore.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.020
Tsurayuki...

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:53.760
I always believed
that I was talented, y'know?

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:56.610
Whether it came
to script writing or novels...

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.010
I thought I could be as good as anyone.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:03.190
But because I like writing,
and am confident about it,

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:06.130
I knew that making
a living off it would be hard.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:08.620
This last year has really
driven that point home.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.960
That's the same as for anyone else, though!

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.260
That's why you wanted to study!
To work hard at it!

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.750
I thought that was the case, too.

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:21.220
That everyone started out
not knowing what they're doing.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:24.770
Until I met you, Kyoya.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.520
Before... me?

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:32.610
At first, you were smiling all the time,
so I just thought you were a nice guy.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:38.160
But then that smile hid a kind
of strength I had no idea about.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:42.530
Every time I screwed up,
or didn't rise to the challenge,

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:45.840
you were there to make
the rational, accurate call.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:48.920
You were guiding us like
it came naturally to you.

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:51.410
You're like a hurdle that I can't get past.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:54.910
"There's no way I can catch up
to the way this guy thinks."

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:58.950
I wondered how many times I'd have
to redo life to get on your level.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:03.610
But you weren't a writer.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:07.590
That's why I thought
I could work with you.

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:13.320
Work part-time, earn my tuition,
and stick to you.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:18.870
But I collapsed, like a dumbass,
and you saved me again.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:21.890
You ran around, setting everything up...

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.160
You basically handled everything.

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:28.630
And I wasn't able to do a thing about it.

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:30.080
That's...

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:35.260
But you said it was all on us.
That we deserved the praise.

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:39.340
I couldn't believe how defeated
and lost that made me feel.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:40.720
No...

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:45.870
I realized how I couldn't
accomplish anything without you.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:48.050
"I can't stay here."

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:51.480
That was the moment
that it became clear to me.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:52.360
You're wrong!

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:57.710
I... I had faith in your writing, Tsurayuki.

00:18:57.710 --> 00:19:01.830
That's why I was trying to figure out
a way to put a spotlight on it!

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:06.500
I couldn't have done any of this
without you, either!

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.660
I wouldn't be so sure about that.
I bet you could've pulled it off.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.470
"We're going to figure
something out, damn it."

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:16.240
You've made miracles happen
after saying that before.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:17.490
It's not...

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:20.560
I wasn't... I just...

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:26.170
I had a pen name in mind,
for after I became a writer.

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:30.090
The family name was going to be
from my hometown.

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:34.230
It might not have the best relationship
with it now, but I did grow up there.

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:37.430
And for the given name, Kyoya...

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:41.200
I was thinking of taking the way your name
is pronounced for part of it.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:45.910
Kawagoe Kyoichi.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:54.740
As in, "Kyoya is number one."

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.480
Pretty good, right?

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:00.510
Well... Take care of yourself, Kyoya.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:25.660
Why? What did I do wrong?

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.400
Hashiba-kun, what's wrong?

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:37.290
Keiko-san...

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:41.620
Keiko-san, um... Tsurayuki...

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:43.840
I wonder why.

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.800
Why did things turn out like this?

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:49.890
Why?

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:53.350
I just... I wanted...

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:57.920
I wanted to accomplish something
ten years in the future.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:01.120
Which is why I thought this time leap
was my chance for that.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:04.170
I'd go to art school, study,

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:07.820
and create with the Platinum Generation...

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.910
I wanted to help them in their time of need.

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:12.290
But... Huh...

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.540
Their time of need?

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.000
In the future, they had already...

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.690
They were already stars without me.

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:23.170
But after the time leap...

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:26.040
I interfered with their lives,
because I assumed...

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:29.100
And because I did that...

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:34.350
Tsurayuki's... Kawagoe Kyoichi's
future changed?

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:39.420
Wh... What do I do?!
What do I do now?!

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:44.360
Is this really how it oughta be?

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:47.950
Please... Keiko-san... I...

00:21:56.910 --> 00:22:01.670
Y'know, I wonder what would
happen in the future at this rate?

00:22:08.830 --> 00:22:11.940
Huh? What was I doing?

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:16.230
I can't remember.

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:18.600
Daddy!

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:20.210
Ow, ow, ow...

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:21.280
You sleep too much!

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:23.220
Um, who are you?

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:25.860
What do you mean?

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:29.110
Oh, you want me to introduce myself?

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:31.240
Gotta practice, right?

00:22:32.390 --> 00:22:35.910
My name is Hashiba Maki!

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:38.770
Hashiba... Maki?

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:42.380
Who? Do I have a relative named that?

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:44.790
What's wrong, Daddy?

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:47.090
You've been making
a weird face this whole time.

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:49.370
Wait, "Daddy"?!

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:52.350
You're... my kid?

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:56.840
Hey, Mommy! Daddy's acting weird!

00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:55.850
Whoa, wait—

00:22:58.380 --> 00:22:59.790
Where am I?

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:01.850
I know... th-the time...

00:23:01.850 --> 00:23:03.760
I'll check my phone. Come on...

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:06.280
May 13th (Sun)

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:08.440
That's... It can't be!

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:11.910
What do you mean about
Daddy being weird, Maki-chan?

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:15.990
He keeps acting like he
doesn't know who I am!

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:19.730
He's playing a prank on you!

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:21.760
Isn't he a naughty daddy?

00:23:22.470 --> 00:23:25.520
Good morning, Daddy.
You certainly slept a lot.

00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:26.840
It's already afternoon.

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:30.770
Dad...

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:33.860
Kyoya-kun? What's wrong?
